Package: mrwin
Title: Scalable Causal Win Statistics for Hierarchical Composite Endpoints
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Nguyen Thien", "Minh", email = "minhnt@ump.edu.vn", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Causal win-statistic methods for hierarchical composite endpoints
    in Mendelian randomization. Estimates a dose-standardised causal win ratio
    by forming polygenic-score strata, computing adjacent-stratum
    instrument-standardised gradients, and pooling them by generalised least
    squares. Provides a subquadratic, compiled hierarchical win/loss kernel for
    biobank-scale data, an analytic influence-function variance as a fast
    alternative to the multiplier bootstrap, Fieller confidence intervals for
    the ratio estimand, optional ordinal inverse-probability-of-treatment
    weighting, and step-down pleiotropy ('MR-Egger') diagnostics.
